  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Envelope Layers**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the envelope\'s construction. First up, I\'m defining the layers, starting with the back, or the inner lining. Its position is at z-0, and the plan is to style it with a lovely Gabby\'s pastel pattern, such as a soft pink.\n\n\n**Defining Card Positioning**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how the letter card behaves within the envelope. When closed, it\'s completely hidden inside, tucked away with no visible text or imagery. It\'s positioned with `z-10`. During opening, the card elegantly slides upward above the envelope, with `z-30` or `z-40`, to appear in front of the flap and pocket. The goal is to make a smooth and dramatic transition.\n\n\n**Detailing Flap Properties**\n\nI\'ve been further refining the envelope\'s flaps. I\'m focusing on their positioning and styling, defining the right and bottom flaps. I\'ve given them crisp pastel colors and a subtle shadow on the bottom flap. The most recent focus is the top flap\'s dynamic behavior, specifically its Z-index adjustment when opening to ensure the letter card appears correctly on top. I\'m finalizing its rotation and z-positioning based on the open/closed state.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now nailing down the final z-index values to ensure perfect layering. The wax seal sits at z-35, triggering a flap unfold animation and a celebratory confetti display on click. I\'m double-checking the visual order: back at z-0, open top flap at z-5, closed letter at z-10, front pocket flaps at z-20, closed top flap at z-25, and open letter at z-30. I\'m also confirming proper CSS 3D configuration.\n\n\n"
